39906.6 gpu: world lighting-control control=dynamicLighting kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=73 triangles=45927 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant, not a material key: the pixel shader replaces the lightmap-only factor with 0.62+0.38*dot(normal, lightDirection) for 73 visible materials / 45927 visible triangles; no VMT declares it, so every surface is shaded by the same guessed direction and the baked lightmap's own direct light is counted twice; off
39906.6 gpu: world lighting-control control=specular kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=73 triangles=45927 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant: one lobe (boost 0.12, exponent 32) for 73 visible materials / 45927 visible triangles; no visible material declares $phong, so the lobe is added to materials that never asked for one; off
39906.6 gpu: world lighting-control control=bump kind=pass-switch state=refused declared=23 visible=20 resolved=23 missing=0 materials=20 triangles=17977 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=COALMINES/BLENDGROUNDTOGRASS_COALMINES resource=materials/Nature/dirtground006_height-ssbump.vtf reason=off: the world pass has one bump sampler slot (--world-bump) and the per-material path is off too (--world-material-bump), so the 20 visible materials that name one of 18 distinct $bumpmap textures are drawn with no normal map at all
39906.6 gpu: world lighting-control control=$bumpmap2 kind=material-key state=refused declared=1 visible=1 resolved=1 missing=0 materials=1 triangles=8610 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=COALMINES/BLENDGROUNDTOGRASS_COALMINES resource=materials/Nature/dirtground003_height-ssbump.vtf reason=$bumpmap2 is layer 2's normal map: it is lerped into layer 1's normal by the vertex blend weight, so it is sampled only when --world-material-bump and --world-bump2 are both on; with either off it is refused, not silently replaced by layer 1's; 1/1 of those materials also declare $ssbump, so their second-layer texel is a bumpBasis weight and stays refused even with both switches on (--world-bump2-texture measures the layer with a diagnostic normal map instead)
39906.6 gpu: world lighting-control control=%detailtype kind=material-key state=refused declared=20 visible=14 resolved=0 missing=20 materials=14 triangles=6846 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=WOOD/WOOD_FLOOR002 resource=materials/overlays/detail006.vmt reason=detail layers are the --world-detail switch: the detail material's $basetexture is sampled at the atlas uv scaled by $detailscale and combined with the albedo by $detailblendmode; with the switch off the layer is refused; 20 of 20 referenced detail VMTs are absent from this install, so the layer's own texture and blend mode cannot be resolved here; %detailtype is a key in the material that names the layer, not in the detail VMT, and is read above; %detailtype names a detail-prop group that VBSP consumes at map compile time (it emits prop_detail sprites and models there), so the key never reaches a runtime shader and has no consumer here
